{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 51, :comments ["<b>Because you trespassed against Me.</b> You caused a trespass to be committed against Me." "<b>Because you did not sanctify Me.</b> You caused that I would not be sanctified — I had said to you, ״וְדִבַּרְתֶּם אֶל הַסֶּלַע״ (Numbers 20), but they struck it, and needed to strike it twice. Had they spoken to it and it would have given its waters without being struck, the name of Heaven would have been sanctified — for Israel would have said: If a rock, which is not subject to reward or punishment — if it merits, it receives no reward, and if it sins, it is not punished — fulfills the commandment of its Creator thus, then we, all the more so."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:34.275665858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}